Scope (CC BY 4.0)
-----------------

  data/eval1/, data/eval2/, data/eval3/, data/eval5/, data/eval6/worlds/
      Authored benchmark inputs: synthetic company briefs, coupled-world briefs
      and task files, the four eval-5 consulting scenarios (dataset v1.0) and
      the eval-6 world histories and task files.

  private/eval1/, private/eval2/, private/eval3/, private/eval5/, private/eval6/
      Scorer and oracle material: world specifications, calibration reports,
      certificates, answer keys, check registries, golden probes, scoring
      seeds, as-run pins and CANARY.txt files.

  Evaluative text prompts, wherever they sit
      The prompt, brief and judge text, including the text held as strings in
      dbwm/eval*/prompt.py, dbwm/eval1/brief.py, dbwm/eval6/d3/brief.py and
      dbwm/eval6/d2_judge.py. The code around that text is MIT.

  README.md, CHANGELOG.md and the Markdown files under docs/
      Documentation prose. Code blocks and commands inside them may also be
      used under MIT.

